<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>{{title}}</title>
{{{stylesheets}}}
</head>

<body class="{{pdfulator_features}}">

  <article>

    <!-- RUNNING-CONTENT SLOTS.
         Named by ROLE, not by position: a slot says what it is, and the
         styler decides where it goes. `attribution` can sit bottom-left on
         one theme and top-centre on another without the markup changing, and
         nothing here has committed to a physical side -- which is what keeps
         recto/verso and RTL open rather than needing a second set of slots.
         CSS's sixteen margin boxes are all physical, so a positional name
         here would have to be re-mapped by the styler anyway.

         Hidden from the flow by the stylers (both already hide these), and
         lifted into a margin box by whichever mechanism the paginator has:
         `string-set`/`string()` for Vivliostyle, `position: running()`/
         `element()` for Paged.js.

         THE ids AND .page-* CLASSES ARE COMPATIBILITY ALIASES for the styling
         that already targets them, and are to be removed once both stylers
         address slots by data-slot alone. -->
    <div class="pdfulator-slots">
      <div class="slot page-header-left"  data-slot="running-title" id="pageHeader">{{{title}}}</div>
      <div class="slot"                   data-slot="running-section"></div>
      <div class="slot page-footer-left"  data-slot="attribution" id="pageFooter">{{#copyright}}<span class="footer-copyright">© {{year}} {{copyright}}</span>{{/copyright}}{{#footer}}<span class="footer-text">{{#copyright}}   |  {{/copyright}}{{footer}}</span>{{/footer}}{{#revision}}<span class="footer-revision">{{#copyright}}   |  {{/copyright}}{{^copyright}}{{#footer}}   |  {{/footer}}{{/copyright}}{{revision}}</span>{{/revision}}{{^copyright}}{{^footer}} {{/footer}}{{/copyright}}</div>
      <div class="slot page-footer-right" data-slot="page-number"></div>
    </div>

    <hgroup>
      <h1 class="doc-title">{{{title}}}</h1>
      {{#subtitle}}<p class="doc-subtitle">{{{subtitle}}}</p>{{/subtitle}}

      {{#authors}}
      <address class="doc-author">
        <span class="author-name">{{name}}</span>{{#affiliation}}<span class="author-affiliation">{{affiliation}}</span>{{/affiliation}}{{#email}}<span class="author-email"><a href="mailto:{{email}}">{{email}}</a></span>{{/email}}
      </address>
      {{/authors}}

      {{#project}}<div class="doc-project">{{project}}</div>{{/project}}
      {{#date}}<time class="doc-date">{{date}}</time>{{/date}}
      {{#revision}}<div class="doc-revision">{{revision}}</div>{{/revision}}
    </hgroup>

    <main>
      {{{body}}}
    </main>

  </article>

</body>
</html>
